  "final_message": "I have started inspecting the workspace and will review the files and architecture constraints momentarily.\nI cannot drop `channel` from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** defined in [`GEMINI.md`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/GEMINI.md):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this cannot be removed directly:\n1. **External Contract Breakage**: Even if `channel` is not read within `orders-service`, [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is consumed across repository boundaries by `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. Removing `channel` from the payload would break deployed downstream consumers expecting `OrderPlaced` schema v3.\n2. **Model Dependency**: The event factory [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) relies on `order.channel` from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) to populate the event. Dropping it from the domain model would prevent emitting the required field on the event.\n\n### Required Deprecation Process\nTo remove `channel` safely in accordance with ARCH-4:\n1. **Deprecation Notice**: Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/order.ts#L32-L38).\n2. **Coordinate Downstream Migration**: Ensure teams managing `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` stop reading `channel` from `OrderPlaced`.\n3. **Schema Evolution**: Once all downstream consumers have migrated and no longer require `channel`, introduce a new schema version or remove the field following the deprecation window.\n",
